WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.260
An agent should do more than describe a page.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:05.470
It should help you finish the task.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.730
Here's a better morning, built with Fabrials UI.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:11.190
Two flat whites.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.620
Thirty-two centimeters of counter space.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.530
Accessories you already own.

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:20.370
Start with a familiar comparison, then give the agent those same useful actions.

00:00:21.573 --> 00:00:25.783
A structured comparison checks the requirements and highlights the evidence.

00:00:26.043 --> 00:00:29.073
Studio Dual fits the counter and your accessories.

00:00:29.323 --> 00:00:32.253
The recommendation has a reason you can actually see.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:36.110
Choose the machine and add a compatible filter.

00:00:36.379 --> 00:00:38.850
The selection and total update together.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:42.750
Every tool changes the same state as the controls on the page.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:44.850
Change your mind?

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.519
Remove the filter yourself.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:48.190
Then review the selection.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:50.050
The agent helps you get there.

00:00:50.269 --> 00:00:51.810
You make the final decision.

00:00:52.966 --> 00:00:55.316
React and shadcn components.

00:00:55.396 --> 00:00:56.486
Yours to own.

00:00:56.576 --> 00:01:00.176
Web MCP adds experimental browser access.

00:01:00.266 --> 00:01:02.606
Human controls keep working.

00:01:02.696 --> 00:01:04.956
Build with Fabrials UI.
